From dc69aaccb089b784249ae19845986e72cfaa0594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:39:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Settings] The settings laid out by what goes out: HDR
 or SDR first, then Dolby Vision, then the rest

Users found settings that govern one thing in different places: "Adjust
display HDR mode" (Kodi's) in Player > Videos, and "Play HDR videos as SDR",
which it greys out, at the Expert level of System > Display (forum thread
30682, #175); and asked for the output to come first and what depends on it
after (#195). Reading the groups showed more of the same: the SDR target of
every HDR video in the Dolby Vision group, between the content mapping v4.0
and its two children; the wide colours of SDR among Kodi's dither and colour
management; the notice of the playback mode and Kodi's own player
information in the HDR group; the mapping to a projector after four other
settings it does not govern.

No setting id changes, so every value that a user set stays as it was: Kodi
keeps a setting by its id, not by its place (CSettingsManager), and 1.1
reads the same guisettings.xml.

System > Display, in this order:
- General (Kodi's), then Kodi's whitelist, which is about modes and refresh
  rates and was after five groups of HDR.
- HDR: "Adjust display HDR mode", moved from Player > Videos, with a help of
  Hades' own (#62502) that says what Off does here: HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG go
  out as SDR, while native Dolby Vision still goes out as Dolby Vision, and
  how to have that as SDR too. "Play HDR videos as SDR" under it, as its
  child, at the Advanced level like it (was Expert). The SDR target with its
  custom white and gamma, the gamut of the SDR made of HDR, and "Keep the
  wide colours of SDR videos". The brightness and gamma of the GUI in HDR.
- Dolby Vision: the output first (native, the menus, Low-Latency with its
  settings, HDMI 1.4b, the converter, the Radeon), then what the TV gets
  (trims, content mapping v4.0 with its two children right under it).
- Other videos as Dolby Vision (a new group, #62500): HDR10+, HDR10
  measured, HLG, and videos with both Dolby Vision and HDR10+.
- HDR on displays without Dolby Vision, and projectors: Dolby Vision as
  HDR10 and its mapping to the display together, then HDR10 adapted, scene
  by scene, and the luminance told.
- HDR colour depth and format, with its one Advanced setting first.
- The Dolby Vision engine, Stereoscopic 3D and Calibration as they were.

Player > Videos: a group "Player information" (#62501) with the notice of
the playback mode and Kodi's own player information, from System > Display.
Player > Subtitles: a group "Stereoscopic 3D" with the depth of subtitles
over 3D video (Hades' and Kodi's), which applies to text and picture
subtitles alike and was in the group of the text styles. System > Audio:
"Surround sound through this USB-C adapter or hub" after the list of
passthrough formats, which it cut in two.

The texts that named the old places follow: the help of "Play HDR videos as
SDR" (#61111, which also said that every HDR video goes out as SDR with
Kodi's setting off, which is not so for native Dolby Vision), the hint of the
player information (#52597, Advanced level now), and the help of the
Radeon's Dolby Vision (#61093), whose check moves to "Check this setup" in
the LibreELEC settings. English first, then es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
